# Electron main-process environment variables.
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# These are loaded by `dotenv` at app startup (see main.js).
# They are NOT exposed to the React renderer; for renderer env vars edit
# ../vitt-overlay-react-client/.env (VITE_-prefixed keys only).
#
# Windows portable builds: place `.env` next to the portable `.exe` so the app
# can pick it up at runtime (PORTABLE_EXECUTABLE_DIR).
#
# Windows SmartScreen: unsigned portable builds show a security warning.
# To remove it, sign the build before distributing:
#   set WIN_CSC_LINK=path\to\certificate.pfx
#   set WIN_CSC_KEY_PASSWORD=your-cert-password
#   npm run dist:win:portable
